meta {
  name: Create Job
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{serveUrl}}/config/jobs/{{jobName}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "node": "node-1",
    "driver": "hello",
    "driver_config": null
  }
}

docs {
  Adds or replaces the job {{jobName}} (common.JobConfig) in the config
  served by `realm serve`. The name is taken from the path; a `name` in the
  body is optional but must match it.

  A whole new config is instanced with the job before replacing the current
  one, so any config error (unknown node or driver...) is rejected and the
  current config is kept.

  Jobs are not part of the cluster state, so the change is neither planned
  nor rolled out.

  Responses: 201 created, 200 replaced, 400 invalid job or config.
  Body: the job.
}
